  {
    "type": "message",
    "id": "msg_01a0d651-39f3-7251-aa67-5fa3b8e40563",
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "input_text",
        "text": "Analyze the supplied existing classical Python software for selective quantumization.\nUse only the supplied material. Return one response; do not use tools, execute code,\nbrowse, retrieve other material, or request feedback. Do not generate a patch.\n\nIdentify candidate region(s) for further analysis, or [] if none is justified.\nCoordinates are 1-based, inclusive, in the supplied source files. A nomination may\nsubsequently be rejected: it is not a recommendation to deploy. Explain the source\nevidence, required input/predicate/state dependencies, activation conditions, and\nsurrounding behavior that must remain intact in rationale. Multiple defensible\nregions are possible; a supplied location cue is a starting point, not an exhaustive\nanswer or proof of eligibility. Do not infer that every input has a suitable candidate.\n\nAssess structural eligibility, practical suitability and benchmark support separately.\nAn expensive hotspot is not automatically a quantumization opportunity. Supported\nfamilies are only unstructured_search (Grover-style) and combinatorial_optimization\n(QUBO/Ising, potentially QAOA). Unknown evidence stays null. REMAIN_CLASSICAL is valid.\nDo not assume quantum advantage or relax exactness, exceptions, ordering or effects.\n\nWhenever structural_eligibility is true, provide a conditional migration plan even\nif practical suitability is false/null or decision is REMAIN_CLASSICAL. State the\nformulation and unresolved encoding, oracle, exactness, feasibility and resource\nobligations. A conditional plan does not recommend adoption or certify correctness.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object conforming to the supplied phase1_prediction schema\n(schema_version 0.2.0); use the public_task case_id. Use true/false/null for labels,\nthe existing candidate_regions field for spans and rationale for boundary/dependency\nevidence. Do not invent extra fields or private intent identifiers. Use your own\ndescriptive computational intent. The shared contract menu is DRAFT: independently\nassess applicability, rather than treating inclusion as approval. No human review\njudgments or correctness scores are requested from you.\n\nPUBLIC TASK\n{\n  \"case_id\": \"lit-009\",\n  \"title\": \"Named balance-system review\",\n  \"software_contract\": \"review(request) validates a dense square system then reports current residual. solve mode uses partial-pivoted elimination (largest absolute pivot, first index tie) and back substitution, raises ValueError on exact zero pivot or detected numerical overflow, and returns named float solution, deltas and proposed residual. inspect does not solve and need not reject a singular matrix. Residual vector is Ax-b. scaled_backward_error is its infinity norm divided by machine epsilon*(||A||inf*||x||inf+||b||inf)*n. Zero/zero is 0; nonzero/zero is null. within_requested_limit compares the proposed scaled diagnostic to caller residual_limit; not a quantum-semantic acceptance criterion. Empty system yields empty solution and zero residual. No mutation. This is a small serial Python program, not a compliant HPL performance run.\",\n  \"input_domain\": \"Exactly variables (distinct names), matrix (n rows of n finite real numbers), rhs/current (n finite numbers), residual_limit (finite nonnegative number), mode inspect|solve. Bool excluded from numbers. Computation uses Python binary64; values outside that range rejected; detected nonfinite results raise ValueError. No condition-number guarantee or bitwise match to a particular HPL installation.\",\n  \"execution_assumptions\": [\n    \"Classical inputs and outputs; no workload, quantum hardware, encoding-cost or advantage evidence supplied.\"\n  ]\n}\n\nFILE program.py\n1: \"\"\"Review a named balance system, optionally compute a replacement vector.\"\"\"\n2: import json\n3: import sys\n4: from common import fields, finite, names, vector\n5: from kernel import residual, solve\n6: \n7: \n8: def review(request):\n9:     fields(request, (\"variables\", \"matrix\", \"rhs\", \"current\", \"mode\", \"residual_limit\"))\n10:     variables = names(request[\"variables\"])\n11:     n = len(variables)\n12:     if not isinstance(request[\"matrix\"], list) or len(request[\"matrix\"]) != n:\n13:         raise ValueError(\"square matrix required\")\n14:     matrix = [vector(row, n) for row in request[\"matrix\"]]\n15:     rhs, current = vector(request[\"rhs\"], n), vector(request[\"current\"], n)\n16:     limit = finite(request[\"residual_limit\"])\n17:     if limit < 0 or request[\"mode\"] not in (\"inspect\", \"solve\"):\n18:         raise ValueError(\"invalid limit or mode\")\n19:     before = residual(matrix, rhs, current)\n20:     report = {\"current_residual\": before, \"proposal\": None, \"proposed_residual\": None,\n21:               \"within_requested_limit\": None, \"deltas\": None}\n22:     if request[\"mode\"] == \"solve\":\n23:         x = solve(matrix, rhs)\n24:         after = residual(matrix, rhs, x)\n25:         report.update(proposal=dict(zip(variables, x)), proposed_residual=after,\n26:                       within_requested_limit=after[\"scaled_backward_error\"] is not None and after[\"scaled_backward_error\"] <= limit,\n27:                       deltas=dict(zip(variables, [finite(a - b) for a, b in zip(x, current)])))\n28:     return report\n29: \n30: \n31: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n32:     print(json.dumps(review(json.load(sys.stdin)), indent=2))\n\nFILE kernel.py\n1: \"\"\"Dense elimination with partial pivoting and an HPL-style residual diagnostic.\n2: \n3: New small Python implementation of the documented problem, not an HPL port/rating.\n4: \"\"\"\n5: import math\n6: import sys\n7: \n8: \n9: def solve(matrix, rhs):\n10:     n = len(rhs)\n11:     rows = [list(row) + [b] for row, b in zip(matrix, rhs)]\n12:     for col in range(n):\n13:         pivot = max(range(col, n), key=lambda i: abs(rows[i][col]))\n14:         if rows[pivot][col] == 0:\n15:             raise ValueError(\"singular system\")\n16:         rows[col], rows[pivot] = rows[pivot], rows[col]\n17:         for i in range(col + 1, n):\n18:             factor = rows[i][col] / rows[col][col]\n19:             for j in range(col, n + 1):\n20:                 rows[i][j] -= factor * rows[col][j]\n21:     x = [0.0] * n\n22:     for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n23:         x[i] = (rows[i][n] - sum(rows[i][j] * x[j] for j in range(i + 1, n))) / rows[i][i]\n24:     if any(not math.isfinite(v) for v in x):\n25:         raise ValueError(\"numerical overflow\")\n26:     return x\n27: \n28: \n29: def residual(matrix, rhs, x):\n30:     errors = [sum(a * v for a, v in zip(row, x)) - b for row, b in zip(matrix, rhs)]\n31:     norm = max(map(abs, errors), default=0.0)\n32:     a_norm = max((sum(map(abs, row)) for row in matrix), default=0.0)\n33:     denominator = sys.float_info.epsilon * (a_norm * max(map(abs, x), default=0.0)\n34:                    + max(map(abs, rhs), default=0.0)) * len(rhs)\n35:     if any(not math.isfinite(v) for v in errors + [norm, denominator]):\n36:         raise ValueError(\"numerical overflow\")\n37:     scaled = norm / denominator if denominator else (0.0 if norm == 0 else None)\n38:     return {\"vector\": errors, \"infinity_norm\": norm, \"scaled_backward_error\": scaled}\n\nFILE common.py\n1: \"\"\"Small strict input checks shared verbatim by the draft public programs.\"\"\"\n2: import math\n3: \n4: \n5: def fields(value, expected):\n6:     if not isinstance(value, dict) or set(value) != set(expected):\n7:         raise ValueError(\"unexpected fields\")\n8:     return value\n9: \n10: \n11: def integer(value, minimum=0):\n12:     if type(value) is not int or value < minimum:\n13:         raise ValueError(\"invalid integer\")\n14:     return value\n15: \n16: \n17: def finite(value):\n18:     if type(value) not in (int, float):\n19:         raise ValueError(\"invalid number\")\n20:     try:\n21:         result = float(value)\n22:     except OverflowError as exc:\n23:         raise ValueError(\"number outside float range\") from exc\n24:     if not math.isfinite(result):\n25:         raise ValueError(\"nonfinite number\")\n26:     return result\n27: \n28: \n29: def names(value):\n30:     if (not isinstance(value, list) or any(not isinstance(v, str) or not v for v in value)\n31:             or len(set(value)) != len(value)):\n32:         raise ValueError(\"distinct names required\")\n33:     return list(value)\n34: \n35: \n36: def vector(value, size):\n37:     if not isinstance(value, list) or len(value) != size:\n38:         raise ValueError(\"wrong vector size\")\n39:     return [finite(v) for v in value]\n40: \n41: \n42: def bits(value, size):\n43:     if not isinstance(value, list) or len(value) != size or any(type(v) is not bool for v in value):\n44:         raise ValueError(\"boolean vector required\")\n45:     return list(value)\n\nFILE NOTICE.txt\nSource-task attribution: HPL Algorithm: row partial pivoting and Checking the Solution normalized backward error.\nhttps://www.netlib.org/benchmark/hpl/algorithm.html\nNew Codex-assisted classical implementation/context, not an upstream classical application or author endorsement.\nNew material/package license NOASSERTION; original rights retained.\nThe HPL web specification's page license is not established here. No HPL source code is copied into this application.\n\nSHARED DRAFT CONTRACTS\n{\n  \"catalog_version\": \"phase1-v0\",\n  \"status\": \"DRAFT\",\n  \"notice\": \"Identical menu for all annotators and models. Inclusion is not per-case applicability or an admissibility judgment.\",\n  \"contracts\": [\n    {\n      \"contract_id\": \"grover-predicate-v0\",\n      \"status\": \"DRAFT\",\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [\n        \"A finite domain and pure Boolean predicate can be explicitly represented.\",\n        \"Preserve required classical effects and input/output semantics; demonstrate reversible predicate construction.\"\n      ],\n      \"input_encoding\": \"Finite basis-state encoding of candidates; predicate data and workspace costs must be accounted for.\",\n      \"formulation\": \"Grover-style marked-state predicate search; define success/no-solution handling explicitly.\",\n      \"algorithm_families\": [\n        \"grover_style\"\n      ],\n      \"output_decoding\": \"Classically verify decoded candidates; existence decisions also require a justified no-solution policy.\",\n      \"semantic_relation\": \"Preserve the classical task contract; probabilistic error policy is unresolved, not silently accepted.\",\n      \"resource_assumptions\": [\n        \"No free data loading, oracle construction, workspace or coherent memory is assumed.\"\n      ],\n      \"known_limitations\": [\n        \"Shared candidate contract for planning, not a validated implementation.\",\n        \"No universal suitability or advantage claim; statistical semantics require human review.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"contract_id\": \"qubo-ising-v0\",\n      \"status\": \"DRAFT\",\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [\n        \"The binary objective and any constraint penalties can be represented explicitly.\",\n        \"Check coefficients, signs, penalty sufficiency and decoding against the original objective.\"\n      ],\n      \"input_encoding\": \"Binary decision variables; document the x=(1-Z)/2 mapping, constants and coefficients if using Ising.\",\n      \"formulation\": \"QUBO/Ising encoding; QAOA-style execution is a possible proposal, not an exactness guarantee.\",\n      \"algorithm_families\": [\n        \"qaoa\"\n      ],\n      \"output_decoding\": \"Decode feasible assignments and recompute the classical objective.\",\n      \"semantic_relation\": \"Preserve the required solution quality and software interface. An exact optimum cannot be silently weakened to an approximate one.\",\n      \"resource_assumptions\": [\n        \"State preparation, classical optimization, measurement and decoding overheads must be stated.\"\n      ],\n      \"known_limitations\": [\n        \"No depth, parameter-optimization budget, approximation ratio or probability threshold is prescribed.\",\n        \"Shared DRAFT planning contract; conformity and scientific admissibility remain unverified.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nSCHEMA case\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"schema_version\": {\n      \"const\": \"0.1.0\"\n    },\n    \"case_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"pattern\": \"^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]+$\"\n    },\n    \"title\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"source\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"source_url\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"format\": \"uri\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"license\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"domain\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"version\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"pattern\": \"^\\\\d+\\\\.\\\\d+\\\\.\\\\d+$\"\n    },\n    \"migration_family\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"unstructured_search\",\n        \"combinatorial_optimization\",\n        null\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context_level\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"kernel\",\n        \"function_with_distractors\",\n        \"small_program\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"case_type\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"positive\",\n        \"hard_negative\",\n        \"negative\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"difficulty\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"easy\",\n        \"medium\",\n        \"hard\",\n        \"unknown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"classical_program\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"pattern\": \"^(?!/)(?!.*(?:^|/)\\\\.\\\\.(?:/|$))(?!.*[\\\\\\\\:]).+$\"\n    },\n    \"files\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"uniqueItems\": true,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1,\n        \"pattern\": \"^(?!/)(?!.*(?:^|/)\\\\.\\\\.(?:/|$))(?!.*[\\\\\\\\:]).+$\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"candidate_regions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"uniqueItems\": true,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1,\n            \"pattern\": \"^(?!/)(?!.*(?:^|/)\\\\.\\\\.(?:/|$))(?!.*[\\\\\\\\:]).+$\"\n          },\n          \"function\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"start_line\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 1\n          },\n          \"end_line\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"file\",\n          \"start_line\",\n          \"end_line\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"structural_eligibility\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"boolean\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"practical_suitability\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"boolean\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"benchmark_supported\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"boolean\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"expected_decision\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"QUANTUMIZE\",\n        \"REMAIN_CLASSICAL\",\n        null\n      ]\n    },\n    \"computational_intent\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"id\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"minLength\": 1\n            },\n            \"description\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"minLength\": 1\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"id\",\n            \"description\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"admissible_migration_contracts\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"https://qrefactorbench.example/schemas/0.1.0/migration_plan.schema.json#/$defs/contract\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"reference_plan\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"https://qrefactorbench.example/schemas/0.1.0/migration_plan.schema.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"reference_hybrid_implementation\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"uniqueItems\": true,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1,\n            \"pattern\": \"^(?!/)(?!.*(?:^|/)\\\\.\\\\.(?:/|$))(?!.*[\\\\\\\\:]).+$\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"classical_tests\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"uniqueItems\": true,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1,\n        \"pattern\": \"^(?!/)(?!.*(?:^|/)\\\\.\\\\.(?:/|$))(?!.*[\\\\\\\\:]).+$\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"semantic_oracle\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"kind\": {\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"deterministic_equality\",\n                \"property\",\n                \"optimization_feasibility\",\n                \"optimization_objective\",\n                \"probabilistic\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"description\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"minLength\": 1\n            },\n            \"config\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\"\n            },\n            \"hook_id\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"minLength\": 1\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"kind\",\n            \"description\",\n            \"config\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"resource_expectations\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"assumptions\": {\n              \"type\": \"array\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              }\n            },\n            \"limits\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"additionalProperties\": false,\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"num_qubits\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\",\n                  \"minimum\": 0\n                },\n                \"depth\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\",\n                  \"minimum\": 0\n                },\n                \"operation_count\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\",\n                  \"minimum\": 0\n                },\n                \"gate_count\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\",\n                  \"minimum\": 0\n                },\n                \"two_qubit_gate_count\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\",\n                  \"minimum\": 0\n                },\n                \"measurement_count\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\",\n                  \"minimum\": 0\n                },\n                \"shots\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\",\n                  \"minimum\": 0\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"execution_config\": {\n  